foreign  violence on the streets of Paris  protesters against police  of tear gas an attempt to push back a  furious crowd  [Music]  angry after a gunman opened fire at a  Kurdish Cultural Center at lunchtime  shooting at least six people  the scene shortly before tensions boiled  over the interior Minister said  investigators would confirm if Kurds  were specifically targeted  it's not clear that this person was  politically active and involved even if  what he did was a characterized attack  against foreigners but it'll be for the  Judiciary investigation to confirm that  the shootings happened in a busy  Multicultural Street in the central 10th  District a 69 year old French man has  been arrested  I can tell you there are three people  dead there are two people in a critical  condition and two people with minor  injuries the perpetrator who has been  arrested was also wounded in the face  officials say he was already known to  police with reports he was linked to a  saber attack on migrants in 2021.  authorities are investigating whether  racism fueled today's killings  to date we do not really know the  motivations of this killer the  investigation is ongoing the  neighborhood is completely cordoned off  I ask all residents and inhabitants not  to go to the neighborhood to those who  are at home to stay there for the moment  the neighborhood will likely be cordoned  off all day  France is still on alert after a string  of deadly attacks by Islamic extremists  in 2015 and 2016.  authorities say there's currently no  indication of a terrorist motive today  and that the gunman acted alone  the president has sent his condolences  to France's Kurds condemning the heinous  killings  [Music]  but the attack has struck at the heart  of this community  people here are demanding answers and  Justice Siobhan Robbins Sky News

